{
  "$comment": "Published components of the Annotation Kit — the library the plugin places notes with, so a rationale is a real library instance rather than a drawn box. `key` is the assetKey to pass to figma.importComponentByKeyAsync, and each property carries the exact `key` that setProperties requires. Captured through use_figma; see scripts/extract.md.",
  "$note": "No annotation component exposes its body text as a component property, so setProperties changes only variants. The text is a plain TEXT layer inside the instance: load its font, then set characters. reference/annotate.md names the layer for each one.",
  "$duplicateNames": "A published name is not unique in this file — `A11y / Annotation / Spec` exists twice with different keys and different variant axes. Those entries are keyed `<name> [<nodeId>]` and carry the true Figma name in `name`. Every other entry is keyed by its name alone.",
